Z||000000||Formula88||02-20-2001||08:47 PM||||Well, took my beast off the road today to begin the clutch swap.  Was originally planning for this weekend, but with the good weather today and the clutch making LOTS of clattering noise, I decided to go ahead and start.  Haven't done much besides pull the deck lid, slave, various sensors, and douse the exhaust crossover bolts with Liquid Wrench.  Gonna have to let that soak overnite.  Just wanted to throw that out.  My 1st clutch change on a Fiero.  Luckily, LZeitgeist is helping me, and he's done it twice on his 88 Formula, so at least ONE of us has some first hand experience on it.  Wish me luck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Me&Pat_Cars.jpg"> <BR>Doin' the clutch on the beast to the left.  That's LZeitgeist's Formula on the right.||||reg||11
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||02-20-2001||09:19 PM||||Good luck...||||reg||1
